Subject: Reduce-Network-Allocation-Pressure

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla networking allocates a new PacketBundle and buffer for every
packet sent, with no pooling. Under high packet throughput (entity
tracking, chunk sends), this creates significant GC pressure that
manifests as tick lag during collection cycles.

Impact:
Lower GC pause frequency and duration under network load. More
stable TPS on servers with many players or high entity density.

Migration Note:
This patch introduces packet buffer pooling using Moonrise's
concurrentutil library. Packet output streams are reused rather
than reallocated per send.
